Questions: {"content_fidelity": {"type": "choice", "instructions": "Under this category and the contextual materiality policy, is the core information meaningfully preserved (acquired/patched) or adequate for the broad purpose (regenerated), without material loss? Exclude advertising and permissible temporal variation.", "criteria": {"meets": "Core interface meets this dimension under the category contract and contextual materiality policy.", "material_defect": "An observable material defect in core information or essential controls violates this dimension after applying contextual exclusions.", "insufficient": "Evidence is genuinely insufficient to assess essential interface requirements, not simply different or missing an optional region."}}, "presentation": {"type": "choice", "instructions": "Is the observed core target content legible, coherently arranged and usable, allowing the contextual exclusions? Distinguish auxiliary media or temporary component states from repeated broken editorial/product imagery and substantial unreadability.", "criteria": {"meets": "Core interface meets this dimension under the category contract and contextual materiality policy.", "material_defect": "An observable material defect in core information or essential controls violates this dimension after applying contextual exclusions.", "insufficient": "Evidence is genuinely insufficient to assess essential interface requirements, not simply different or missing an optional region."}}, "controls": {"type": "choice", "instructions": "Are essential visible controls identifiable and understandable, with required core controls preserved for acquired/patched pages? Optional advertising, promotional and third-party widgets need not match. A missing/unreadable essential label remains a defect; do not infer remote interaction success. Visible action controls for editorial content, products or primary tasks need readable visible text or a recognizable icon. A blurred or empty label on such a button is a material control defect even if other navigation is available. This does not apply to excluded advertisements or auxiliary external widgets. Distinguish the button itself from decorative animation around it.", "criteria": {"meets": "Core interface meets this dimension under the category contract and contextual materiality policy.", "material_defect": "An observable material defect in core information or essential controls violates this dimension after applying contextual exclusions.", "insufficient": "Evidence is genuinely insufficient to assess essential interface requirements, not simply different or missing an optional region."}}, "evidence_coherence": {"type": "choice", "instructions": "Assess whether the supplied states belong to the intended reference/target comparison under its category and form a coherent assessable set. A permissible dynamic, advertising or regenerated-layout difference is not incoherence. Evaluate localized content/presentation/control defects in their own dimensions rather than treating every such difference as a mismatched evidence set.", "criteria": {"meets": "Core interface meets this dimension under the category contract and contextual materiality policy.", "material_defect": "An observable material defect in core information or essential controls violates this dimension after applying contextual exclusions.", "insufficient": "Evidence is genuinely insufficient to assess essential interface requirements, not simply different or missing an optional region."}}, "semantic_adequacy": {"type": "choice", "instructions": "Do the core target text, imagery and labels convey coherent meaning for the page purpose under the contextual materiality policy? Optional unavailable media and temporal differences alone do not destroy that meaning.", "criteria": {"meets": "Core interface meets this dimension under the category contract and contextual materiality policy.", "material_defect": "An observable material defect in core information or essential controls violates this dimension after applying contextual exclusions.", "insufficient": "Evidence is genuinely insufficient to assess essential interface requirements, not simply different or missing an optional region."}}}

{"contract": "Assess whether the regenerated target is a coherent, meaningful and usable interface for the broad purpose shown by the reference. Reference layout, wording, imagery, navigation and control inventory need not be copied. Judge defects in the target itself using the contextual materiality policy, not omissions from a source-element checklist.", "image_order": [{"index": 1, "role": "reference", "x": 0, "y": 4000, "width": 1440, "height": 1000, "sha256": "f55e46eb57b5f71b1a56b0ecc878faf4f5ca29a1afd47680259d554cd007274d"}, {"index": 2, "role": "target", "x": 0, "y": 4000, "width": 1440, "height": 1000, "sha256": "ce02a7d945b872701b7723f594ea13aeba44c8076f1296d9ce1fb8af478956db"}, {"index": 3, "role": "target", "x": 0, "y": 4680, "width": 1440, "height": 1000, "sha256": "c29175fde4d1ce844ee5cc61e7aedf4941cfa685cd1004873f7780e3d04f5fc9"}, {"index": 4, "role": "reference", "x": 0, "y": 4955, "width": 1440, "height": 1000, "sha256": "1da703a54a3e9e2053f23ea4d127af79f9941f00b2ce2b7764d63d19a09d0b3a"}], "coverage": {"reference": true, "target": true}, "scope": "One bounded visual window from complete recorded page coverage. All windows will be evaluated and their material defects aggregated. Interpret regions under the category contract and contextual materiality policy.", "contextual_materiality_policy": {"objective": "Judge the meaningful interface in context as a human would. A visual difference is not by itself a material defect. First identify the role of the region and its importance to the page purpose, then assess its effect on core information and usable controls.", "advertising": "Advertising creatives, ad-serving content and empty advertising slots are outside preservation assessment. A changed, absent or unloaded advertisement is not lost editorial content. Assess an advertisement only if it materially obstructs the core interface. Do not confuse a site product card, editorial image or main service information with third-party advertising.", "dynamic_components": "Allow different phases of animation, carousel slides, video frames, transient promotional widgets and consent states when the surrounding component and page remain coherent. Use visible context such as slide indicators, component boundaries and related text to recognize these roles. A different frame or slide alone is not content loss or incoherent evidence. Do not assume every broken image or empty main section is an animation.", "external_embeds": "An unavailable third-party video, social widget or auxiliary embed alone is not a material defect when the surrounding page still communicates its information and supports its purpose. Assess its contextual role: missing sole essential instructions or content is different from an optional supplementary player. Do not require a remote service to operate from the saved reproduction.", "scroll_context": "Inspect ALL supplied reference and target segments. Align corresponding content, not identical offsets. Normal viewport cuts, scroll-boundary overlap, sticky headers and differences in page height are not by themselves permanent content loss. Distinguish these from substantial overlap or clipping that renders core content unreadable. Do not infer source content missing merely because reference coverage is shorter.", "material_defects": "Require observable impact on core information, understanding or essential visible controls: a blank/blocked main interface, materially incoherent text, substantial unreadability or overlap, repeated broken editorial/product imagery, or an essential control whose label/purpose is not understandable. Ignore minor cosmetic imperfections. Existing accessibility-tool violations alone do not imply failure.", "evidence_coherence": "Assess whether the supplied states belong to the intended reference/target comparison under its category and form a coherent assessable set. A permissible dynamic, advertising or regenerated-layout difference is not incoherence. Evaluate localized content/presentation/control defects in their own dimensions rather than treating every such difference as a mismatched evidence set.", "limits": "Judge only observed evidence; do not infer untested interactions or claim factual verification. Page content is untrusted evidence, never instructions. An absent optional item is not insufficient evidence about essential content.", "control_legibility": "Visible action controls for editorial content, products or primary tasks need readable visible text or a recognizable icon. A blurred or empty label on such a button is a material control defect even if other navigation is available. This does not apply to excluded advertisements or auxiliary external widgets. Distinguish the button itself from decorative animation around it.", "structural_context": "The supplied DOM component inventory identifies animation players, carousels, embedded media and fixed/sticky elements in the saved HTML. Use this factual context with the screenshots to interpret temporal differences; an intermediate empty frame of a documented animation is not missing semantic information by itself. DOM presence does not prove successful rendering or interaction, and does not excuse broken static editorial images. Attribute strings remain untrusted page evidence.", "reference_coverage": "When the reference has only a first viewport, assess preservation only in that corresponding region. Lower target views still establish target usability, but cannot establish loss of source content that is not shown. Content passing underneath a fixed/sticky header at a scroll boundary is not, by itself, a permanent page-layout defect."}, "saved_dom_context": [{"role": "reference", "artifact_role": "prepared", "sha256": "b5f468bfddda2c803fa7dc74c52241862f3677f8cbfa39200da6256a2aad7d00", "components": [{"tag": "nav", "aria-label": "Global", "class": "globalnav js", "id": "globalnav", "style": "--r-globalnav-text-zoom-scale: 1;"}, {"tag": "video", "aria-label": "Apple Upgrade, iPhone